    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nI'm having issues with indentscope in C indents where curly braces are not there. Here's a video:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/31820255/229249581-79cc0914-0f6c-42a8-9e8e-cd12ab2ea283.mp4\r\n\r\nHere's the snippet, just in case:\r\n\r\n```c\r\nint smbios_add_string(u8 *start, const char *str)\r\n{\r\n\tint i = 1;\r\n\tchar *p = (char *)start;\r\n\r\n\t/*\r\n\t * Return 0 as required for empty strings.\r\n\t * See Section 6.1.3 \"Text Strings\" of the SMBIOS specification.\r\n\t */\r\n\tif (*str == '\\0')\r\n\t\treturn 0;\r\n\r\n\twhile (*p) {\r\n\t\tif (!strcmp(p, str))\r\n\t\t\treturn i;\r\n\r\n\t\tp += strlen(p) + 1;\r\n\t\ti++;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tstrcpy(p, str);\r\n\tp += strlen(str);\r\n\t*(p + 1) = '\\0'; // Indicate the end of set with an additional null byte\r\n\treturn i;\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThis is the default behaviour.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIndent guides should not be shown on empty lines, for non-bracketed blocks in C.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIndent guides are also shown for empty lines, even if the block is not bracketed.",
