            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I do understand that, but is it expected behaviour for it to show indent on empty lines? Here is what it looks like, with  `try_as_border = false`.\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/31820255/229270847-d55b5ba4-ee3b-47d9-b5cc-3c7ac0b2ec2e.mp4\r\n\r\nThe video shows that the if block ends on line 157, but the indent guides are still shown for it on line 158. It feels a bit off while using it.\r\n\r\nHere is my `lazy.nvim` config:\r\n```lua\r\n  {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.indentscope\",\r\n    opts = function(_, opts)\r\n      return vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", opts, {\r\n        draw = {\r\n          animation = require(\"mini.indentscope\").gen_animation.none(),\r\n        },\r\n        options = {\r\n          try_as_border = false,\r\n        },\r\n        symbol = \"a\",\r\n      })\r\n    end,\r\n  },\r\n```",
